# EAS upload manifest — read by BOTH `eas deploy` (web hosting) and `eas build` (native).
#
# ⚠ EAS uses this file INSTEAD OF .gitignore, not in addition to it: "If you create a .easignore
# file, the EAS CLI prioritizes it over the .gitignore file." So every .gitignore rule that must
# keep holding has to be repeated below — that is why `node_modules/` and `.env` appear here even
# though git already ignores them. Before this pass the file was one line, which was correct for
# `eas deploy` and would have had the first native build upload node_modules (646 MB) and the
# whole design reference alongside the app.
#
# `dist/` is deliberately NOT ignored. `eas deploy` uploads the exported web build from there, and
# inheriting .gitignore (which ignores dist/) is what made the live site 404 every static asset —
# the Welcome logo + onboarding slate backgrounds + favicon all vanished. A native build therefore
# also carries dist/ (~73 MB). That is waste, not breakage; keeping the web deploy working wins.
#
# `node_modules/` is unanchored, so it also covers the vestigial dist/assets/node_modules/ that the
# previous version of this file existed to exclude.

# --- repeated from .gitignore: never upload ---
node_modules/
.expo/
web-build/
.env
.kotlin/
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
src/domain/training/ingest/out/
/Scratch/
/_repo-audit/
index_extract_tmp.txt
legacy-design-test.zip
.design-sync/

# --- authoring sources and reference material: nothing in src/ imports them (verified by grep) ---
Docs/
Programs/
design_reference/
ds-bundle/
